- op: discuss  # 0adc
  at: '2026-08-27T23:11:49Z'  # 0adc
  by: agent  # 0adc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0adc
  clock: 5  # 0adc
  nonce: 0adc  # 0adc
  message: "TWO NEW SINK-SIDE INSTANCES, found while deriving 0006's useful precision for WI-gibom.\nSection A of 0006 looked only at SOURCES; both of these are sinks, and both are\nself-disclosed in the catalogue's own notes, so they need no new evidence:\n\n  1. erlang io_lib:format declared under logging. erlang.yaml's own note on that row:\n     \"Returns iolist, not direct I/O, but typically written immediately.\" The primitive\n     performs no I/O; the value is returned in-process. Same shape as newIORef -- a name\n     credited for a boundary it does not cross. All three of rabbitmq's headline TPs land\n     on it, at 7, 12 and 7 hops.\n  2. python urllib.request.Request declared under net_send, rowed beside urlopen and\n     urlretrieve. Request is a CONSTRUCTOR; it builds a request object and sends nothing.\n\nNEITHER WAS DEDUCTED from the 24.1% figure, and the reasons differ:\n  - Request: in jaeger's scripts/release/notes.py every Request(...) is consumed by\n    urlopen(req) on the next line (L34/36, L39/41, L86/88, L116/119, L196/198), so the\n    network boundary really is crossed. Attribution defect, not a vacuous claim.\n  - io_lib:format: the landing site of a 7-to-12-hop chain could not be traced from 0006's\n    packets (its family-F defect searches for sink sites only inside the SOURCE symbol's\n    span, so the sink listing is structurally empty for every multi-hop situation).\n    ADR-0046's conservative default therefore holds, and it is published as declared\n    sensitivity S3 (3 TPs; deducting them alone gives 21.4%).\n\nTHE OPEN PYTHON/ELIXIR ROWS ARE NOW SIZED on 0006's population, which may help price the\nvocabulary ruling this item defers:\n    argv (parse_args + sys.argv) under env_read ....... 10 of 38 headline TPs -> 15.2%\n    Application.get_env / application:get_env ......... 5 of 38 -> 19.6%\n    both resolved against ............................. 15 of 38 -> 10.7%\nErlang application:get_env is the same function as the elixir row this item names, so it\ntravels with it. plausible#3 is NOT in that set: numeric_ids.ex reads\nSystem.get_env(\"NUMERIC_IDS_*\"), a genuine process-environment read.\n\nCONFIRMED PAYING: the bash half this item already fixed is 6 of the 11 deductions --\ncert-manager#0/#1/#2/#3, spacedrive#6, guacamole-client#3 were all \"> /dev/null\"-only and\nwere live when 0006 ran. And this item's two DID-NOT-REPRODUCE findings (\">&2 counts\",\n\">> reported as >\") are now struck from 0006 section A rather than left standing."  # 0adc
- op: discuss  # 90b4
  at: '2026-08-28T07:14:15Z'  # 90b4
  by: agent  # 90b4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 90b4
  clock: 6  # 90b4
  nonce: 90b4  # 90b4
  message: "SWEEP DONE, 2026-08-28, dev fa65f2352f. This closes the gap the item names in\nits own last line (\"no fix is proposed here and the per-language row counts are\nnot enumerated ... the catalogue has not been swept for others\"). Full write-up\nand reusable instrument: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nular_sweep_08282026/\n(RESULT.md, census.py, census.json). Run through the PRODUCTION loader, not by\ngrepping YAML.\n\nTHE CENSUS THAT HAD NEVER BEEN TAKEN: 3051 rows / 3011 distinct primitives\nacross 15 catalogues; 29 multi-boundary; 2989 SINGLE-boundary rows, which is\nthis item's population. Per-language counts in RESULT.md section 1.\nCROSS-VALIDATION: the 29 matches INV-vaduk's independent multi-boundary census\nexactly (29 primitives, 17 with a discriminator, 12 with nothing). Two\ninstruments built for different questions agree, which is what licenses the 2989.\n\nTHIS ITEM'S OWN SIX INSTANCES, RE-VERIFIED AT TIP -- TWO OF SIX STILL REPRODUCE:\n  LIVE          haskell IORef/STRef -> db_read\n  LIVE          c socket -> net_recv\n  FIXED         bash '>' with no target check      (#541, 7fe8758338, io_target_kind)\n  FIXED         bash BASH_SOURCE -> env_read       (#541; absent from every catalogue)\n  NOT A DEFECT  python parse_args -> env_read      (INV-tutar)\n  NOT A DEFECT  elixir Application.get_env -> env_read (INV-tutar)\nINV-tutar's resolution DEFINES env_read as \"an ambient CONFIGURATION read\n(environment variables, system properties, argv)\", membership being the\nCAPACITY to carry a credential. argv and application config are inside that\ndefinition, so the statement should stop citing them. I am not editing the\nstatement unilaterally; flagging it.\n\nNON-REPRODUCTION OF FOUR SAMPLED INSTANCES IS NOT EVIDENCE THE INVARIANT HOLDS.\nIt is evidence the sample was small. Status stays violated.\n\nTHE TWO LIVE INSTANCES ARE NOT INSTANCES, THEY ARE FAMILIES -- and the sweep\nfound a third that was never filed. Filed as instances, each isbefore this item:\n  WI-rigut  P1  haskell in-process cells (IORef/STRef/MVar/STM) -> db_*  31 ROWS.\n                This is the mechanism behind 0006's vacuous TPs: all five\n                shellcheck true positives are real dataflow filed under\n                untrusted-input-no-database against haskell in-process refs.\n                haskell.yaml already records the doubt in its own notes and does\n                not resolve it.\n  WI-dosov  P2  connection lifecycle -> net_recv, 10 LANGUAGES. c's net_recv row\n                is [socket, bind, listen, accept, recv, recvfrom, recvmsg];\n                socket/bind/listen receive NOTHING. `accept` deliberately NOT\n                folded in -- it returns the peer address, which is\n                network-controlled, so it needs its own ruling.\n  WI-hikut  P2  query BUILDERS -> db_read, 5 LANGUAGES, ~18 rows, NOT previously\n                filed. JPA/JDBC create*, all nine Ecto.Query combinators, django\n                order_by/distinct. None contacts a database; each returns a\n                builder, and the executors are SEPARATELY rowed, so one logical\n                read is credited twice. The catalogue states the defect in its\n                own notes: \"part of the read path\". Being on the read path is\n                not performing the read.\n\nINSTRUMENT LIMITS, STATED BECAUSE THEY BOUND THE NUMBER. Every stratum\nUNDER-collects -- the constructor regex missed all nine Ecto.Query combinators,\nthe handle-name set missed bind and listen; both were found by reading the rows\nthe strata did surface. So ~62 candidate rows is a FLOOR, not an estimate. It\nalso OVER-collects, load-bearingly: objc NSData.initWithContentsOfFile: and\nscala Source.fromFile match \"constructor declared as a read\" and are entirely\ncorrect. Every stratum is a candidate list, hand-adjudicated here.\n\nA GATE BEAT A GREP, AGAIN. My first pass read c.yaml with an awk range,\nconcluded net_recv was empty, and recorded the socket instance as FIXED. The\nrange pattern matched only the section header. The production loader returned\nthe row. The wrong instrument exited 0 and produced a plausible CLOSURE, which\nis the expensive direction.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT CLAIM: nothing here prices the three families in precision\npoints. F1 is linked to five 0006 TPs by the refuters' own write-up; F2 and F3\nhave no measured finding attached. Pricing needs a cohort exercising JDBC/JPA,\nEcto and haskell concurrency, and that cohort is not assembled."  # 90b4
