  message: "DONE in PR #602 (dev a738c503b9). Measured A/B, 7 repos, per-arm cache, arms\nsequential, each arm proven live by a row-count canary (NEW 181 / OLD 219).\n\n  SENSITIVE  UNTRUSTED-NO-HOST-FS evidence rows  27 -> 7 (-74%)\n  CONTROL    HOSTSECRET-NO-HOST-FS rows         154 -> 154 (+0), unmoved\n             per-repo too (7, 100, 8, 32, 4, 1, 2)\n  CONTROL    all 11 untouched boundaries identical across arms\n\nATTRIBUTION READ OFF THE OLD ARM'S EVIDENCE, not inferred from totals.\nFull write-up: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nular_ab_08282026/RESULT.md"  # ccdd
- op: discuss  # e147
  at: '2026-08-28T10:51:20Z'  # e147
  by: agent  # e147
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e147
  clock: 8  # e147
  nonce: e147  # e147
  message: "SECOND SWEEP PASS SHIPPED (PR #606, dev 4ef65c2f31): F4, lifecycle callbacks and\nclose calls declared as data transfers.\n\nThe first pass looked for constructors declared as READS. It never looked at\nlifecycle. REMOVED: WebSocket.onopen / WebSocket.onerror / EventSource.onerror\n(net_recv -- the open event carries no data and the error event is SPECIFIED to\ncarry none, so a cross-origin failure cannot leak why); Network.Socket.close\n(net_send -- a FIN is not a payload any line of the program produced, and\nnet_send is a SINK, so the row accepted a tainted value as \"sent\");\nNetwork.Socket.gracefulClose (net_recv -- THE SUBTLE ONE: it really does read,\ndraining until EOF, but returns unit, so no byte reaches the program, and\nnet_recv under the auto-source map means a source of data the program USES).\n\nKEPT, and the distinction is what makes the removals defensible:\nWebSocket.onclose. A CloseEvent carries `code` and `reason`, both chosen by the\npeer, so it genuinely delivers peer-controlled data. Removing all three\n\"lifecycle\" callbacks together would have been the tidy answer and the wrong one.\n\nMOVED, NOT DELETED: BroadcastChannel.postMessage carried TWO defects in one row\n-- it SENDS and was declared net_recv (a direction error minting untrusted_input\nat a call that emits) and the channel is not network in either direction. Both\nsides move to ipc_*. Moving keeps the send REPRESENTED; deleting would lose a\nsink, the false-all-clear direction. The receive label is unchanged because\nipc_recv and net_recv both derive untrusted_input.\n\nTHE DUPLICATE-KEY LOAD GATE CAUGHT ME TWICE writing this -- a second `ipc_send:`\nsection and a second `notes:` on one row, both silently last-wins under plain\nPyYAML. That gate came out of THIS item, and it earned its keep on its own\nauthor.\n\nSTILL OPEN ON THIS CLASS: WI-lunav (sink-side builders -- NOT F3's mirror; needs\nargument-position adjudication, not row removal). The 2989 single-boundary rows\nare enumerated but only partially adjudicated: the strata in census.py are\nsyntactic proxies and every one of them under-collects."  # e147
- op: discuss  # 8805
  at: '2026-08-28T11:06:52Z'  # 8805
  by: agent  # 8805
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8805
  clock: 9  # 8805
  nonce: '8805'  # 8805
  message: "F4 MEASURED AFTER THE FACT, AND IT IS INERT. Write-up:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nular_f4_ab_08282026/RESULT.md\n\nI shipped F4 (#606) before measuring it. F1-F3 were measured before merge; F4\nwas not, and \"measure, then say so\" has no exemption for the last family. Doing\nit afterwards is the correction, not a substitute for the right order.\n\nRESULT: zero delta everywhere. 4 repos, per-arm cache, arms sequential, canary\non WebSocket.onopen (OLD present / NEW absent).\n  net_recv chains (the touched boundary)  31 -> 31\n  every other boundary                    identical\n  taint verdicts                          unchanged\nTHE COHORT IS NOT THE PROBLEM: all four contain the identifiers in source (nest\nonopen x1 onerror x2, phoenix-framework 7/8, squoosh onerror x20, simplex-chat\nNetwork.Socket x4).\n\nWHY: NEITHER ARM MATCHED A SINGLE F4-RELEVANT PRIMITIVE. The rows were\nunreachable before they were removed. `ws.onopen = handler` is a property\nASSIGNMENT, so no method-construct call edge exists for a method-kind row to\nmatch. INV-linub's \"capability is not recall\" one level over. F4 is therefore a\ncatalogue-CORRECTNESS change with no behavioural effect on this cohort -- the\nrows minted nothing because they matched nothing.\n\nTHIS CORRECTS A JUSTIFICATION I SHIPPED. #606 argued the removal was safe\n\"because onmessage still carries the receive\". onmessage is an assignment\nproperty too, so that reasoning was WRONG AS STATED. The conclusion survives on\na different basis -- WebSocket.addEventListener is a genuine method call and is\nstill rowed -- and that is what actually carries the receive. Filed as WI-zumoz.\n\nNOT MEASURED, and not to be read as zero: BroadcastChannel (no cohort repo uses\nit, so the ipc_send direction fix is unmeasured) and gracefulClose (appears\nnowhere in the cohort).\n\nTWO FINDINGS SURFACED AND FILED:\n  WI-zumoz (P3) three surviving javascript rows are unreachable by construction.\n  WI-budiv (P2) six Phoenix/Plug RESPONSE SENDERS declared net_recv -- and\n    unlike F4's rows these MATCH LIVE, so that defect is active. It mints\n    untrusted_input at a call that emits AND leaves the egress unregistered as a\n    sink, which is the false-all-clear direction."  # 8805
- op: discuss  # abdd
  at: '2026-08-28T12:05:01Z'  # abdd
  by: agent  # abdd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # abdd
  clock: 10  # abdd
  nonce: abdd  # abdd
  message: "STATUS AFTER THE 08-28 SWEEP. Six families adjudicated and shipped; the item\nstays VIOLATED, and the reason is a number rather than a feeling.\n\nSHIPPED (each measured, each with a control in the same run):\n  F1 WI-rigut  haskell in-process cells -> db_*                31 rows  #602\n  F2 WI-dosov  socket/bind/listen -> net_recv, 10 languages    21 rows  #602\n  F3 WI-hikut  query BUILDERS -> db_read, 5 languages          18 rows  #602\n  F4           lifecycle callbacks + close -> transfers         7 rows  #606\n  F5 WI-budiv  Phoenix/Plug RESPONSES -> net_recv              26 rows  #609\n  F6           erlang stdin reads -> logging                    3 rows  #610\nAggregate A/B (F1-F3, 7 repos): UNTRUSTED-NO-HOST-FS 27 -> 7 evidence rows\n(-74%) with the control claim HOSTSECRET unmoved at 154 -> 154 and every\nuntouched boundary identical. F5 separately: net_recv 53 -> 14, net_send 20 ->\n58, and on a NETWORK claim plausible went violated(4) -> violated(7).\n\nWHY IT STAYS VIOLATED. The census found 3051 rows / 2989 SINGLE-BOUNDARY. I\nadjudicated on the order of 100. The strata that found these families are\nSYNTACTIC PROXIES for a semantic property and every one of them under-collects\n-- demonstrated twice: the constructor regex missed all nine Ecto.Query\ncombinators, and the handle-name set missed `bind` and `listen`. The root cause\n(\"rows bind a name to a kind with no verification\") is unchanged for the\nremaining ~2900.\n\nWHAT IS NOW MECHANICALLY CHECKED, which is the only part that scales. A DIRECTION\nGUARD runs in CI: any primitive whose NAME is unambiguous about direction sitting\nunder a boundary of the opposite direction fails, unless it is declared\n`simultaneous` (exempted BY PROPERTY, not by list). That is one dimension of\n\"kind checked against semantics\" made automatic. It found F6 on purpose after F5\nwas found by luck.\n\nTHE THREE THINGS I LEARNED THAT SHOULD SHAPE THE REST:\n  1. THE MECHANISM IS SHARPER THAN THIS ITEM'S TITLE. db_read/net_recv are\n     AUTO-DERIVED TAINT SOURCES, so a misdeclared row does not merely mislabel\n     -- it MINTS taint at a call that observes nothing.\n  2. THE SINK SIDE IS NOT THE SOURCE SIDE'S MIRROR. Removing a builder declared\n     db_read deletes taint it INVENTED; removing one declared net_send deletes a\n     sink that RECEIVED the tainted value, and nothing carries taint from builder\n     to executor, so the crossing ends up represented NOWHERE. The rule is \"IS\n     THE CROSSING STILL REPRESENTED\" -- which is why Django's lazy QuerySet, JS\n     createServer and the Phoenix router DSL are all KEPT. (WI-lunav.)\n  3. A ROW CAN BE PRESENT, CORRECT-LOOKING AND STRUCTURALLY UNMATCHABLE. F4 was\n     INERT because `ws.onopen = handler` is an ASSIGNMENT, so no method-construct\n     edge exists for a method-keyed row to match. (WI-zumoz.)\n\nOPEN INSTANCES: WI-lunav (P2, sink-side builders -- needs argument-position\nadjudication, NOT row removal), WI-zumoz (P3, three unmatchable javascript rows).\nSTANDING SENSITIVITY NOT TAKEN: io_lib:format/fwrite declared `logging` while\nthe row's own note says \"Returns iolist, not direct I/O\" -- 0006 quantified it\n(useful precision would go 24.1% -> 21.4%). Not fixed here because whether\nremoval loses the finding depends on taint propagating through the intermediate\niolist, which I did not measure."  # abdd
