  message: "2026-09-03: WI-suhug shipped (PR #743) -- io.WriteString / fmt.Fprint* dual, writer-stamped, `pipe`/`net_stream` in the vocabulary. The 0012 gocryptfs row (plaintext -> cmd.StdinPipe()) now classifies ipc_send when the pipe binding is visible in the enclosing function. The c.yaml `unistd.write` note calling write(STDOUT_FILENO) an ipc_send was NOT followed: `_WRITE_TARGET_KIND_BOUNDARY` maps std_stream -> logging per WI-dutah; the note is the stale sibling and still reads that way -- a one-line yaml notes edit for whoever next touches c.yaml (not done here to keep this PR's catalogue diff to go). Six-repo A/B: 29 moved / 0 removed; the vacuous class's three rows are now: WriteString fixed (rowed + stamped), sendmsg (c) untouched -> WI-baran, hPutStrLn (haskell) already declared undecidable and now GATED by the generalised rule (its stamp, when haskell stamps writes, will select logging)."  # 0fab
- op: discuss  # 7e69
