  by: agent  # 7e69
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7e69
  clock: 17  # 7e69
  nonce: '7e69'  # 7e69
  message: "RE-CHECKED AT TIP, 2026-09-04, dev ef9c55f8bf. Nothing has moved on this item since the WI-suhug entry of 2026-09-03; recording that as a positive check rather than leaving the silence ambiguous, plus one loose end that is still where it was left.\n\nTHE c.yaml NOTE FLAGGED ON 09-03 IS STILL STALE. That entry said the ipc_send note calling write(STDOUT_FILENO, ...) an IPC send \"is the stale sibling and still reads that way -- a one-line yaml notes edit for whoever next touches c.yaml (not done here to keep this PR's catalogue diff to go)\". At tip, c.yaml:154 still reads: \"write(STDOUT_FILENO, ...) or write(STDERR_FILENO, ...). INV-vaduk: exactly one of fs_write/ipc_send/net_send is true per call and the fd's nature is established where it was opened.\" WI-dutah (shipped 05-13, c/rust/js/elixir) rules terminal output logging, and WI-suhug's _WRITE_TARGET_KIND_BOUNDARY maps std_stream -> logging. c.yaml's last commit is 26d2995302 (2026-08-31, WI-lipis), which PREDATES the flag, so the edit is still owed. It is a documentation defect with a behavioural tail: c has no write-side target-kind stamp yet (that is WI-baran, still open), so the row is not merely mis-noted -- it is the row a c stdout write can still select.\n\nTHE OPEN MEMBERS NAMED IN THE STATEMENT, verified in the catalogue at tip:\n  haskell IORef/STRef/MVar under db_*   FIXED -- rows deleted, with the rationale written into haskell.yaml at the deletion site (F1/WI-rigut, #602).\n  c socket/bind/listen under net_recv   FIXED -- removed, rationale in c.yaml:100-102 (F2/WI-dosov, #602).\n  bash > and BASH_SOURCE                FIXED (#541); two of the six filed bash claims did not reproduce and are recorded as such.\n  python argparse parse_args env_read   UNCHANGED at python.yaml:666-668, and now carrying a note that RULES it (\"Reads sys.argv, consistent with the sys attribute row in this section\") rather than leaving it unexamined.\n  elixir Application.get_env env_read   UNCHANGED at elixir.yaml:230-232, note \"Application config reads (compile-time + runtime)\". Not adjudicated either way by the 08-28 sweep.\nSo of the six instances the statement enumerates, four are resolved and two remain -- one ruled-and-kept, one genuinely untouched. The statement is not rewritten here because the item's own reason for staying violated is the unswept remainder, not this list.\n\nSTATUS UNCHANGED: violated, P1. The 08-28 entry's reason still governs -- 3051 rows censused, on the order of 100 adjudicated, and the syntactic strata that found the six families are proxies that demonstrably under-collect. Open sub-items unchanged: WI-lunav (P2), WI-zumoz (P3), WI-baran (c, todo_hard/P2 -- its stated dependency, WI-suhug's pipe/net_stream vocabulary, shipped 09-03 in #743, so it is unblocked in fact; the dependency was never recorded as an isbefore link and still is not, which is why nothing surfaced it), and the standing io_lib:format sensitivity."  # 7e69
